The two extra requests are left out of this node.

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI, and the world has no filesystem capability, so the component cannot write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the node's declared `HTTPClient` allowlist. The host would trap on that call, which would fail the whole run. The query would also send input text to a service the node was not granted.

Either feature would need a new declared capability on the node, and I have not added one. The output is unchanged.

I also check each URL's host against the allowlist before fetching. An out-of-list URL becomes a `FetchFailure` and does not trap the run.

